 DevOps Interview Preparation
2–4 Years Experience | Advanced CI/CD – Interview Questions

🔹 CI/CD Fundamentals (Advanced Level)

• What makes a CI/CD pipeline production-ready?
• How do you design pipelines for scalability?
• CI vs CD vs Continuous Deployment
• Pipeline as code — why is it important?
• How do you handle secrets in CI/CD?

🔹 Jenkins – Advanced Questions

• Jenkins master vs agent architecture
• Declarative vs scripted pipeline — when to use what?
• How do you secure Jenkins?
• Jenkins shared libraries — use cases
• How do you handle parallel stages?
• Jenkins pipeline failed intermittently — how to debug?
• How do you manage Jenkins credentials securely?

🔹 GitHub Actions – Advanced Questions

• GitHub Actions workflow architecture
• Hosted runners vs self-hosted runners
• How do you secure GitHub Actions secrets?
• Reusable workflows — benefits?
• Matrix builds — when to use them?
• How do you control workflow permissions?
• GitHub Actions failing only on PRs — why?

🔹 GitLab CI – Advanced Questions

• GitLab CI architecture
• GitLab runners — shared vs specific
• How do you secure GitLab CI pipelines?
• Caching vs artifacts — differences
• Parent-child pipelines — use cases
• GitLab pipeline optimization techniques
• GitLab pipeline stuck in pending — reasons?

🔹 Pipeline Optimization & Reliability

• How do you reduce pipeline execution time?
• How do you handle flaky tests?
• Pipeline fails after deployment — rollback strategy?
• How do you implement approval gates?
• Canary & blue-green deployment via pipelines

🔹 Real-World CI/CD Scenarios

• Pipeline works locally but fails in CI — why?
• Secrets accidentally exposed in logs — immediate action?
• Pipeline triggered multiple times unexpectedly — fix?
• Rollback needed during peak traffic —
pipeline approach?
• Multiple teams using same pipeline — how to manage?

 Interview Tip:
If you explain design decisions + failure handling, interviewers know you’ve worked with real CI/CD systems.
